 `priority` is optional (`normal`). Answers 201 with the new ticket, whose status is `open`. The requester is notified
 that the ticket was received.
 
+### Import tickets: `POST /tickets/import`
+
+```json
+{ "tickets": [ { "title": "VPN drops every hour", "requester": "maria@example.com", "priority": "high" } ] }
+```
+
+Creates many tickets at once, for the move from another tracker. Each item is what `POST /tickets` takes, and there are
+at most 5000 of them. The tickets are created in the order given, each as `POST /tickets` would create it: it is audited
+(with the `X-Actor`) and its requester is notified that it was received. It is all or nothing: when any item is invalid,
+nothing is created and the answer is 400 `invalid`, whose message names the first invalid item by its index in the array
+(`tickets[0]` is the first). Answers 201 with `{ "created": 3, "ids": ["T-0042", "T-0043", "T-0044"] }`, the ids in the
+order of the items. The body may be up to 16 MiB, whatever `MAX_BODY_BYTES` says.
+
 ### List tickets: `GET /tickets`
 
 | Parameter | Meaning |
